# Scene
trueqbit with Claude (Opus 5.5), 2026-11-21: the prerequisites check leaves
the published configuration.

# Decided
- trueqbit: check_prerequisites.h is not part of sqlite_orm_config.h, so
  code can test sqlite_orm's features without the C++17 #error; both
  variants of sqlite_orm.h include it right after prologue.h.
- trueqbit (b): check_prerequisites.h keeps its own copy of the guarded
  <version>/<ciso646> include rather than including stdlib_features.h (it
  reads only the standard's __cpp_lib_*) or a shared header: <version> is
  a given since C++20, and the fallback goes once C++20 is the baseline.
  Marked "on purpose:"; the exception is trueqbit's, so the mark is settled.
- The <version> block is guarded with defined(__has_include): a toolchain
  short of C++17 evaluating __has_include(...) unguarded fails on that line.

# Discussed
- Preprocessor check, g++-16/clang++ with a stub sqlite3.h (created in the
  same wsl call - /tmp does not persist across calls): SQLITE_ORM_* sets of
  both published headers identical at C++17/20/26; at C++14 the config
  raises 0 #errors (was 2), sqlite_orm.h still 2.
- Not pinned by a test: the suite builds at C++17+; a CI step preprocessing
  the config at -std=c++14 was offered, not added.
